  "reason": "Account locked after 5 failed password attempts. All failures came from the corporate network (203.0.113.10) during New York business hours, interleaved with successful sign-ins from the same network. Matches KB-001 user or saved-password pattern, no hosting or foreign sign-ins. Requesting unlock for the ticket sender."
}

{
  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hola Tom, revisamos tu cuenta. Los intentos fallidos vinieron de la red de la oficina en horario laboral, sin señales de un ataque, así que es probable que una contraseña antigua guardada en algún dispositivo (por ejemplo, el correo de tu teléfono) esté causando el bloqueo. Hemos enviado la solicitud de desbloqueo a un técnico para que la apruebe. Una vez aprobada, podrás volver a iniciar sesión con tu contraseña actual. Cuando puedas, actualiza la contraseña guardada en tu teléfono y en cualquier otro dispositivo para que la cuenta no se vuelva a bloquear. Si no logras entrar hoy o la cuenta se bloquea de nuevo, responde a este ticket y lo escalaremos.",
  "internal_note": "User: Tom Becker (user_id 4, Finance, America/New_York, usual hours 09:00-17:00). Account status: locked, 5 failed_login_count, must_change_password false, not disabled, sign_in_blocked false, VPN enabled. Password last set 2026-07-23. Sign-in logs (14 days): 5 failed_password events, all from corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York during business hours, interleaved with successful Duo-push sign-ins from the same IP. No hosting, foreign, or overnight attempts. Matches KB-001 user or saved-old-password pattern. Queued unlock_account (approval_id 1), pending technician approval. No password reset requested since user remembers password per ticket context (not confirmed). Follow-up: confirm user updates saved passwords on phone and other devices; if account locks again within an hour, escalate per KB-001 and check for stale-credential sources. Ticket was in Spanish; reply written in Spanish.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-001"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
